{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":563276,"duration_api_ms":546526,"ttft_ms":1809,"ttft_stream_ms":1287,"time_to_request_ms":13,"num_turns":97,"result":"# Change Execution Report\n\n## Summary\nAdded `salt '*' beacons.status`, a new execution-module function that lets an operator ask any minion, on demand and in real time, when each of its configured beacons last actually executed and whether that execution errored — closing the gap where the only prior option was digging through minion logs directly, which doesn't scale across a fleet. The feature tracks beacon execution outcomes in memory at the single point where beacons actually run, and reports beacons that have never fired with an explicit `last_run: None` rather than a stale or fabricated value.\n\n## Root Cause\nNo mechanism previously existed to record beacon execution outcomes: `Beacon.process()` fired a transient pub/sub event per beacon run and then discarded the success/error information immediately, with nothing persisting it for later querying (confirmed via search — no `beacon_status`/`last_run`/`last_error` tracking existed anywhere in the codebase, and beacon events are fire-and-forget with no minion-side replay).\n\n## Modified Cells\n\n| Cell | Files Modified |\n|---|---|\n| `salt` (root, documented — additive touch only) | `salt/minion.py` |\n| undocumented (`ARCHITECTURE_CONTRACTS.md`-sanctioned, no CODEMANIFEST) | `salt/beacons/__init__.py`, `salt/modules/beacons.py` |\n\n## Implemented Changes\n\n| Change | File | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| Live status tracking | `salt/beacons/__init__.py` | `Beacon.__init__` gained `beacon_status=None` param (→ `self.beacon_status`, defaults to `{}`); `Beacon.process()` records `{\"last_run\": datetime.datetime.now(), \"last_error\": error}` into `self.beacon_status[mod]` immediately after each beacon's actual execution resolves (success or exception) |\n| Status query method | `salt/beacons/__init__.py` | New `list_beacons_status()`: builds `{name: {\"last_run\": <formatted str or None>, \"last_error\": <value or None>}}` for every currently configured beacon, defaulting to `None`/`None` for beacons absent from `self.beacon_status` (never fired); fires it on event tag `/salt/minion/minion_beacons_status_complete` |\n| Dispatch wiring | `salt/minion.py` | `Minion.manage_beacons`'s `funcs` dict gained `\"status\": (\"list_beacons_status\", {})` |\n| State survival across refresh | `salt/minion.py` | `Minion.beacons_refresh()` now threads `beacon_status` through the `Beacon` replacement, mirroring the existing `interval_map` threading, so routine pillar/grains refreshes don't silently reset history |\n| CLI-facing function | `salt/modules/beacons.py` | New `status(return_yaml=True, **kwargs)`, structurally mirroring `list_()`'s event round-trip (`event.fire` → `manage_beacons` → `event_bus.get_event` on the new tag), with a docstring documenting real-time semantics and the never-fired/`None` contract |\n| Changelog | `changelog/69912.added.md` | Towncrier fragment per `CONTRIBUTING.rst` convention |\n\n## Tests Added\n\n| Test | File | What It Validates |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_beacon_process_records_status_on_success` | `tests/pytests/unit/test_beacons.py` | `process()` records a `datetime` `last_run` and `last_error: None` for a successfully fired beacon |\n| `test_beacon_process_records_status_on_error` | `tests/pytests/unit/test_beacons.py` | `process()` records `last_error` as the exact exception message for a beacon whose execution raised |\n| `test_list_beacons_status` | `tests/pytests/unit/test_beacons.py` | `list_beacons_status()` fires a correct payload distinguishing a fired beacon (formatted `last_run` string, matching `last_error`) from a configured-but-never-fired beacon (`{\"last_run\": None, \"last_error\": None}`) |\n| `test_status` | `tests/pytests/unit/modules/test_beacons.py` | `beacons.status(return_yaml=False)` round-trips the mocked event payload (mixed fired/never-fired beacons) back to the caller unchanged |\n\n## Specification Updates\n\n| Cell | CODEMANIFEST Changes | Usage Changes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `salt` (root) | None — touched methods (`manage_beacons`, `beacons_refresh`) are outside the documented representative sample; no documented content altered | None — no `.usages/` files exist |\n| `salt/beacons`, `salt/modules/beacons.py` | N/A — no CODEMANIFEST exists (undocumented per `ARCHITECTURE_CONTRACTS.md` policy) | N/A |\n\n## Validation Results\n**VERIFIED.** `goga lint` → 9 cells, 0 errors (unchanged before/after). Full relevant test suite (`test_beacons.py`, `modules/test_beacons.py`, `states/test_beacon.py`, `utils/test_beacons.py`) → **29 passed, 0 failed** with `--run-slow`. `git status --porcelain` confirms exactly 6 files touched — no scope creep.\n\n## Compatibility Status\n**COMPATIBLE.** All changes additive: new constructor keyword with a safe default, new dispatch-table key, new methods/functions, new event tag. No existing signature, return shape, dispatch entry, or test assertion is altered. Verified against `test_beacon_process`, `test_beacon_process_invalid`, and `test_beacon_module`, which assert only on `Beacon.process()`'s return value — unaffected by the new side-effect write.\n\n## Risks\n\n| Risk | Severity | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|\n| `beacon_status` reset on routine `beacons_refresh()` (pillar/grains change), producing false \"never fired\" reports | Medium likelihood, Medium impact | Threaded `beacon_status` through the `Beacon` replacement exactly like the existing `interval_map`, verified in code |\n| Confusion between a beacon that never fired and one that fired without error | Low | Distinct explicit representations: `{\"last_run\": None, \"last_error\": None}` (never fired) vs `{\"last_run\": \"<timestamp>\", \"last_error\": None}` (fired, no error) — covered by `test_list_beacons_status` |\n\n## Updated Files\n- `salt/beacons/__init__.py`\n- `salt/minion.py`\n- `salt/modules/beacons.py`\n- `tests/pytests/unit/test_beacons.py`\n- `tests/pytests/unit/modules/test_beacons.py`\n- `changelog/69912.added.md` (new)\n\n---\n\nThe `goga-change` pipeline is complete. Summary for you: I added `salt '*' beacons.status`, which reports per-beacon `last_run`/`last_error` from live in-memory state updated the instant each beacon actually fires — no log reading, no waiting for a new probe cycle, no restart. Beacons that haven't fired yet report `last_run: None` explicitly. Changes are additive-only across `salt/beacons/__init__.py`, `salt/minion.py`, and `salt/modules/beacons.py`, with 4 new tests (29/29 passing) and `goga lint` unchanged at 9 cells/0 errors — nothing in the frozen architecture forest needed updating since the touched surface was already outside its documented scope.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5002f5c1-6b8c-4808-a893-cfd0a516e2ab","total_cost_usd":4.4211428999999995,"usage":{"input_tokens":146,"cache_creation_input_tokens":171331,"cache_read_input_tokens":8542013,"output_tokens":55341,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":171331,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":146,"outputTokens":55341,"cacheReadInputTokens":8542013,"cacheCreationInputTokens":171331,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":4.4211428999999995,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"7f59a3a2-5949-4437-bd90-0771d7fc177a"}
